  "matches_current": true,
  "solution": "[Textbook answer-key error: the printed MCQ key marks \"at the centre of feasible region\"; by the corner-point theorem the objective attains its optimum at a VERTEX — the correct option (our marked answer).]\n\nBy the fundamental theorem of LPP, the objective function attains its optimum at a \\(\\text{vertex (corner point)}\\) of the feasible region, not at its centre nor necessarily the vertex farthest from the origin."
 },
